ce\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786406673052\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The plugin pass is an api.js mechanic: installControl checks the registry after every control activates — selector entries install at el.querySelector(selector) scoped to the host element; selectorless entries attach a hidden headless div to the host. No control embeds a dev:plugins div; dev.plugins is just the registry home (list_plugins).\",\n    \"detail\": \"Registry fetched once per page, single-flight, err -> empty (anonymous pages simply have no plugins). Plugins get their own pass (grafts on grafts); nesting capped at 4 data-nb-plugin ancestors against cyclic registries. Selector scoping changed from document-global to host-element — entries must target selectors inside their target control. Entries apply on the next page load, same as ever.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786409801876\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Both web transports inject EVERY request field into a command's params as nn_<key> — nn_sessionid is just the one the author-defaulting uses; nn_session (the whole session object), headers-derived fields, etc. are equally available to any command that declares them.\",\n    \"detail\": \"HTTP: app/exec puts nn_sessionid into args after check_auth; websocket: the cmd handler copies all request fields as nn_* into params before dispatch (app/service/init.rs). Declared params are REQUIRED by the generated wrapper, so a command declaring nn_* still works on the web (injected) but CLI/MCP callers must pass it explicitly (\\\"\\\").\",\n    \"tags\": \"frontend,bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786411233530\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.code.set_timer fails under `newbound exec` (add_timer needs the `system` globals that only init_globals creates) - run it through `newbound mcp` instead.\",\n    \"detail\": \"The failure is late: the timer component record and the control's timer entry are already written when add_timer panics, and the _patches journal entry is skipped. Re-running the same set_timer over mcp replaces the record and journals normally (replace-only semantics heal the partial write). Observed 2026-08-11 wiring dev.code.init.\",\n    \"tags\": \"set_timer, exec, mcp, globals\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786419691108\n  }\n]\n","old":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"A String return rides the exec envelope's msg with status ok even for ERROR:-prefixed texts — branch on the prefix and relay it verbatim\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.github,envelope\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.3\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"A File return streams only on the app-command route /<app>/<cmd>?k=v; /app/exec answers the file PATH as JSON\",\n    \"detail\": \"store.appCmdUrl builds such links; the archive panel's zip download depends on this.\",\n    \"tags\": \"app,archive,envelope\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.3\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"list_control_patches returns newest-FIRST — two probe harnesses have failed by reading the wrong end\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.code,journal\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"/app/read answers 500 for the runtime library (store-only, never app-loaded) — read runtime state through dedicated commands (get_meta_identity, dev.plugins.list_plugins)\",\n    \"tags\": \"runtime,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.3\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"groups is SECURITY groups; categorization lives in the tags field via set_tags — never write tags into groups\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,tags,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"