kes a library part of the BUILD, not just the listing.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,build,rebuild,ids,supersede\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner's correction of a reverted mistake, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785944284305\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The flow repo's data/flowlang lags its src/: manual changes were made in the src directory that were never propagated back to the data records, so the shipped records are an old version of the primitives. Do not treat data/flowlang as current.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,drift,stale\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner's correction of a reverted mistake, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785944284307\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Every LLM provider behind agent.llm's resolver accepts exactly ONE system message, and it must be at index 0.\",\n    \"detail\": \"vLLM's chat template answers a system message at any later index — including index 1, ahead of every user turn — with a hard 400: BadRequestError \\\"System message must be at the beginning.\\\" So client-side context injection (recall layer 4's mode pack) must be APPENDED to the existing system message, never inserted beside it. Appending rather than prepending is also the cache-friendly choice: the curriculum stays a stable prefix, so server-side prefix caching still hits. agent.agentloop's chatTurn does this in convo(), which builds a merged COPY — the venue's own messages array is never mutated.\",\n    \"tags\": \"llm,agent,platform-api,wire\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"lib\": \"agent\",\n      \"ctl\": \"agentloop\",\n      \"facet\": \"js\",\n      \"hash\": \"6569fbeed2ace744\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785964641067\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.github.import is the drop-in library install path: given a git URL whose repo has data/<lib> and runtime/<lib> at its root, it clones into repositories/<lib>, symlinks both into the instance, calls load_library then rebuild_lib. dev.github has only import and list — no update or remove; update today is `git pull` in repositories/<lib> plus rebuild_lib by hand. A brand-new FFI root additionally needs `newbound rebuild` + host build + restart before the watcher and initializer know the crate.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,dev.github,install,ffi\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbound_core/src/dev/github/import.rs, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786292476513\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"App discovery and activation: an app is any runtime/<name>/app.properties; activation is membership in the comma-separated `apps` key of config.properties, written by app/settings (which re-runs init_globals — no restart to activate a facet-served app). app.properties' `libraries=` list drives load_library at init. The peer-to-peer alternative to git import is dev/install_lib, which streams the library zip from a peer and copies data/<lib>/_APPS/<app> out to runtime/<app>.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,apps,activation,install_lib\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"flowlang appserver.rs init_globals + newbound_core app/{apps,settings}.rs, dev/dev/install_lib.rs, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786292476516\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Command exposure model (check_security): with security on, a command executes anonymously only if BOTH the library meta's readers and the command record's readers contain 'anonymous'; otherwise the session user's groups must intersect the command's readers, and the 'admin' group always passes. Empty readers on a command record therefore means admin-only — the right default for commands that shell out to sudo.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,security,readers,groups\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbound_core/src/security/security/init.rs check_security, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"