owlang crate's native impls. Presence in the store makes a library part of the BUILD, not just the listing.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,build,rebuild,ids,supersede\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner's correction of a reverted mistake, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785944284305\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The flow repo's data/flowlang lags its src/: manual changes were made in the src directory that were never propagated back to the data records, so the shipped records are an old version of the primitives. Do not treat data/flowlang as current.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,drift,stale\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner's correction of a reverted mistake, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785944284307\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Every LLM provider behind agent.llm's resolver accepts exactly ONE system message, and it must be at index 0.\",\n    \"detail\": \"vLLM's chat template answers a system message at any later index — including index 1, ahead of every user turn — with a hard 400: BadRequestError \\\"System message must be at the beginning.\\\" So client-side context injection (recall layer 4's mode pack) must be APPENDED to the existing system message, never inserted beside it. Appending rather than prepending is also the cache-friendly choice: the curriculum stays a stable prefix, so server-side prefix caching still hits. agent.agentloop's chatTurn does this in convo(), which builds a merged COPY — the venue's own messages array is never mutated.\",\n    \"tags\": \"llm,agent,platform-api,wire\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"lib\": \"agent\",\n      \"ctl\": \"agentloop\",\n      \"facet\": \"js\",\n      \"hash\": \"6569fbeed2ace744\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785964641067\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.github.import is the drop-in library install path: given a git URL whose repo has data/<lib> and runtime/<lib> at its root, it clones into repositories/<lib>, symlinks both into the instance, calls load_library then rebuild_lib. dev.github has only import and list — no update or remove; update today is `git pull` in repositories/<lib> plus rebuild_lib by hand. A brand-new FFI root additionally needs `newbound rebuild` + host build + restart before the watcher and initializer know the crate.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,dev.github,install,ffi\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbound_core/src/dev/github/import.rs, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786292476513\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"App discovery and activation: an app is any runtime/<name>/app.properties; activation is membership in the comma-separated `apps` key of config.properties, written by app/settings (which re-runs init_globals — no restart to activate a facet-served app). app.properties' `libraries=` list drives load_library at init. The peer-to-peer alternative to git import is dev/install_lib, which streams the library zip from a peer and copies data/<lib>/_APPS/<app> out to runtime/<app>.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,apps,activation,install_lib\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"flowlang appserver.rs init_globals + newbound_core app/{apps,settings}.rs, dev/dev/install_lib.rs, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786292476516\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Command exposure model (check_security): with security on, a command executes anonymously only if BOTH the library meta's readers and the command record's readers contain 'anonymous'; otherwise the session user's groups must intersect the command's readers, and the 'admin' group always passes. Empty readers on a command record therefore means admin-only — the right default for commands that shell out to sudo.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,security,readers,groups\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbound_core/src/security/security/init.rs check_security, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786292476517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The flowlang builder has three verified gaps around FFI library crates (all worked around, all wanting an upstream flow-repo PR): (1) the default generated Cargo.toml declares serde/serde_json optional deps but omits the serde_support/python_runtime/javascript_runtime feature blocks, so any compile passing --features=serde_support fails until the features are added - which is why the agent/kb/scratch/nebula repos track their crate Cargo.tomls by hand; (2) the generated <ctl>/mod.rs cmdinit is append-only across regenerations - stale command ids accumulate (a delete+re-upsert leaves both generations registered) and the built dylib lags the sources by one compile - the clean reset is delete the generated src dir and run `newbound rebuild`; (3) build_lib answers 'unchanged' when a repo's tracked generated src already matches the store, so rebuild_lib skips the crate build and a fresh install never produces an artifact - dev.github.import/update now build the crate unconditionally.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,flowlang,builder,ffi,bug\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"verified live during the nebula overhaul, 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786295573656\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Store meta.json cargo dependencies are the source the builder regenerates crate Cargo.tomls from - bumping a crate version in a Cargo.toml without updating the owning library's store meta makes every subsequent rebuild silently regress it. The 2026-08-09 flowlang 0.3.31 / ndata 0.3.17 sync had this latent regression via data/app/meta.json (still 0.3.30/0.3.16, masked by Cargo.lock semver compatibility); fixed via save_library_config on the nebula-overhaul branch. Corollary: dev.dev.compile on a newbound_core-rooted library builds only the newbound_core package as an error check - the host binary relink is a separate explicit `cargo build` at the checkout root, per the interim-process restart table.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,build,meta.json,cargo,drift\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"verified live during the nebula overhaul, 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786295580721\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.code.set_groups derives the ENFORCED readers arrays from the groups string at save time, at all three levels: library meta.json; control record plus its inline data records (app.read's gate); command META record (the array check_security reads via lookup_command_id) plus impl record. Empty groups derives [] = admin-only. Returns changed/groups/readers.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Restores the retired editcontrol/editcommand derivation (readers = groups.split(',')). Library-level readers refresh into system.libraries on restart. writers is never touched (only app.delete consults it).\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,set_groups,readers,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-09 (branch claude/dev-ui-security-integration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390464\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"patch_command_body, set_command_imports, and upsert_command preserve existing readers/writers on the records they rewrite; before 2026-08-09 every code edit reset a gated command to admin-only, because flowlang's data::write::write stamps whatever arrays it is passed.\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,readers,dev.code,preservation\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-09 (branch claude/dev-ui-security-integration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390468\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"check_security's group loop passes when the library readers contain 'anonymous' OR the caller's group, so library=anonymous plus per-command groups is the fine-grained convention; check_auth (app.read