ility' too.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,p2p,exec,ids,wire,upsert,patch_command_body,bug\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"live v51 peer panic log from the owner + app.app.exec source + fold2/fold3 verification, 2026-08-11\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786447774149\n  }\n]\n","old":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"A String return rides the exec envelope's msg with status ok even for ERROR:-prefixed texts — branch on the prefix and relay it verbatim\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.github,envelope\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.3\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"A File return streams only on the app-command route /<app>/<cmd>?k=v; /app/exec answers the file PATH as JSON\",\n    \"detail\": \"store.appCmdUrl builds such links; the archive panel's zip download depends on this.\",\n    \"tags\": \"app,archive,envelope\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.3\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"list_control_patches returns newest-FIRST — two probe harnesses have failed by reading the wrong end\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.code,journal\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"/app/read answers 500 for the runtime library (store-only, never app-loaded) — read runtime state through dedicated commands (get_meta_identity, dev.plugins.list_plugins)\",\n    \"tags\": \"runtime,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.3\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"groups is SECURITY groups; categorization lives in the tags field via set_tags — never write tags into groups\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,tags,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.8\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"New dev.code commands are upsert → cargo build → restart (no dylib). Agent-lib commands keep the dylib hot-swap, which can abort mid-request over HTTP — author those over MCP\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.code,upsert_command,mcp\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.6\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"MCP tool discovery (tools/list) depends on the desc field not being blank: a command with an empty desc is omitted from the list entirely, though direct dispatch by lib-control-command name still works. Corollary: every command must carry a desc, or agents browsing the tool list cannot find it.\",\n    \"tags\": \"mcp,discovery,desc\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner, in session, 2026-08-05 — explained why remember/set_tags/set_groups/set_plugin/remove_plugin were missing from tools/list\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785934811069\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The flowlang primitives are part of the MIT-licensed open source flowlang crate. Newbound is not flowlang: flowlang's data/flowlang library must never be committed into newbound's repo. The /data/flowlang gitignore line IS the product and license boundary -- removing it makes those commands part of Newbound, which is not authorized.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,license,boundary,dependencies\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner's correction of a reverted mistake, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785944284303\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Installing a store library whose impl ids duplicate a compiled crate's registrations SUPERSEDES the originals rather than replacing them: at rebuild, newbound generates those commands into its own cmd crate under the same ids, shadowing the flowlang crate's native impls. Presence in the store makes a library part of the BUILD, not just the listing.\",\