n mode) - exec and mcp modes never start timer_loop.\",\n    \"tags\": \"metaidentity, publishapp, boot, dev.code\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786419738826\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"COMMAND IDS ARE THE PEER-TO-PEER WIRE CONTRACT. The jsapi send_* wrappers resolve a command name to the CALLING instance's command id and ship the id to the remote (app.app.exec takes lib + id; the remote does Command::new(db, id) and panics 'Missing file data/...' when the id is absent). Signature compatibility is irrelevant if ids differ. Consequences: (1) NEVER delete_command + re-upsert a command that remote peers call - upsert_command alone already preserves BOTH the command record id and the rust source id for an existing name, so plain upsert is always the id-safe edit; delete-first is only for genuinely retiring a command; (2) dev.code.patch_command_body with an empty old_snippet is BROKEN - it ballooned a 1.8KB source record to 3.7MB of nested content (fold2, 2026-08-11) - use upsert_command for full-body rewrites; (3) save_command requires a live HTTP session (its app_read fails with Key 'data' not found over MCP). This id contract is what broke the owner's first v52 rollout against v51 peers, and retroactively explains the original v44-lineage 'incompatibility' too.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,p2p,exec,ids,wire,upsert,patch_command_body,bug\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"live v51 peer panic log from the owner + app.app.exec source + fold2/fold3 verification, 2026-08-11\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786447774149\n  }\n]","patch_id":"p24","time":1786472610321},{"author":"claude-code","cmd":"","facet":"memory","label":"memory: dev.github.import (and anything reaching flowlang appserver l...","new":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"A String return rides the exec envelope's msg with status ok even for ERROR:-prefixed texts — branch on the prefix and relay it verbatim\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.github,envelope\",\n    \"source\":