ld2/fold3 verification, 2026-08-11\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786447774149\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"flowlang Command::cast_params (0.3.31, command.rs:158) panics on a MALFORMED value for a declared Integer param - parse::<i64>().unwrap() - killing the HTTP handler thread; the 0.3.30 wrapper guard covers only MISSING params. Any UI that builds command URLs from unvalidated DOM values (empty select -> width=, undefined chains, Date arithmetic -> NaN) can panic a thread per request; a retrying poller makes it continuous, which is how the owner hit it in the camera settings preview (2026-08-11). Until fixed upstream, the library-side idiom is: declare URL-facing numeric params as String and parse leniently in-body with a soft-fail (camera does this across snapshot/keyframe/events_page since 228b089); declared-type changes are wire-compatible because query params are strings anyway.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,cast_params,panic,http,params,hardening\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"owner panic report + disposable repro, flowlang 0.3.31 command.rs:158, 2026-08-11\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786472610314\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.github.import (and anything reaching flowlang appserver load_library) cannot run via 'newbound exec' - the exec path skips init_globals(), so load_library panics with \\\"Key 'system' not found\\\"; route such commands through 'newbound mcp' tools/call, which inits globals first.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Observed 2026-08-11 installing mraiser/hollis. src/main.rs: exec branch calls Command::lookup directly; only the mcp branch calls init_globals().\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.github,exec,mcp,init_globals\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786479034893\n  }\n]\n","patch_id":"p26","time":1786490553383},{"author":"claude-code","cmd":"","facet":"memory","label":"memory: flowb rewrites an FFI crate's Cargo.toml dependencies from th...","new":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"A